- **Composer:** removed the text area’s resting border, background, and shadow, leaving the outer plaster frame as the only box. Keyboard focus remains visible.

Both fixes apply in **day and night**. Pictures, weather styling, spacing, and layout are unchanged. The theme was **inactive**, and I left it that way.

The saved CSS is verified; I haven’t seen the rendered result. Please check the toolbar and composer when you next try it.

Reference: `docs/appearance/theme-author-guide.md` — “Hooks.” I also inspected the implementation for toolbar selectors not covered by the documentation.

===== fb4-cafe: Rainy Café has the same two slips as Harbor: check the Library toolbar shapes (search box vs buttons vs view toggle should share one shape) and remove the inner rectangle around the text box in the chat composer. Also: on Home the title and the Conversation/Roleplay/Game/Professor/Widgets buttons sit straight on the busy rainy-window picture with no backing, worst in the light look on a phone. Give them backing per your handbook's words-on-art rule.
